e0$ in [F1]. [given, F1, F3, F4, algebra] 2.1 [Interface traces as characters] For a wave $j$ and $x=(y,0)$ on the interface, $k_j\cdot x=\kappa_j\cdot y$ because $k_j\cdot n$ multiplies the vanishing third coordinate; hence at the interface the tangential trace is $E_j^	au(y,0,t)=\operatorname{Re} igl(e_j^	au e^{i(\kappa_j\cdot y-\omega_jt)} igr)$ and $H_j(y,0,t)=\operatorname{Re} igl(h_j e^{i(\kappa_j\cdot y-\omega_jt)} igr)$, whose normal parts are annihilated by $n	imes\cdot$. The two tangential interface identities of [A1] are identities of tangential vector fields, and for a tangential $w$ the vanishing $n	imes w=0$ forces $w=0$ (in the frame $n=e_3$, $w=(w_1,w_2,0)$ gives $n	imes w=(-w_2,w_1,0)$ by [F3]); hence they say, for all $z=(y,t)\in\mathbb R^2	imes I$, that $\operatorname{Re} igl(A_t e^{i\lambda_t\cdot z} igr)=\operatorname{Re} igl(A_i e^{i\lambda_i\cdot z} igr)+\operatorname{Re} igl(A_r e^{i\lambda_r\cdot z} igr)$ componentwise, with $\lambda_j:=(\kappa_j,-\omega_j)\in\mathbb C^3$ and $A_j=(e_j^	au,h_j^	au)$; equivalently $\operatorname{Re} igl(A_i e^{i\lambda_i\cdot z}+A_r e^{i\lambda_r\cdot z}-A_t e^{i\lambda_t\cdot z} igr)=0$ on the nonempty open set $\mathbb R^2	imes I$, by the additivity of the real part in [F4] and the componentwise linearity of the tangential projection in [F3]. [given, A1, step 1.1, F3, F4, algebra] 3.1 [Frequency grouping] Group the three frequencies of step 2.1 by value: let $
